{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>הכה</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and the others: הוכה כעשב (Isaiah 15:6) and ויבש לבי (Psalms 22:15). הוכה אפרים — through the epidemic plague that was among them. And the end of the verse (Psalms 22:15) — כי שכחתי מאכול לחמי — for through eating my bread I strayed and clung to Ba'al Pe'or, as stated in the Midrash: they set up inns for them selling varieties of food and drink. And similarly הוכה אפרים through Pe'or, as stated at the beginning of the parashah (ibid.): המה באו בעל פעור וינזרו לבושת etc."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The phrase וסיפיה דקרא ('the end of the verse') introduces the Psalms 22:15 quotation, reading it as a midrashic allusion to the sin at Pe'or; 'ibid.' in the final citation refers to Numbers 25:3."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:12.391272334Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}